  "resolution_criteria": "This question will resolve as the date on which OpenAI, or any subsidiary that is primarily responsible for developing ChatGPT, begins trading public shares on a U.S. national securities exchange.",
  "fine_print": "If ChatGPT is renamed or is otherwise succeeded by a new model, the new model will qualify as \"ChatGPT\" for the purpose of this question.",
  "background": "[OpenAI](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/OpenAI) has been moving towards an [Initial Public Offering](https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Initial_public_offering) (IPO) where its for-profit subsidiary OpenAI Group PBC may be listed on a public stock exchange.&#x20;\n\nDuring 2026, it has been reported that OpenAI is [aiming to raise](https://www.forbes.com/sites/investor-hub/article/openai-ipo-things-to-know/) at least \\$60 billion with a valuation of \\~\\$1 trillion. If OpenAI is successful in raising that amount of money, it would be the among largest IPOs in history, potentially exceeded only by SpaceX's recent IPO.\n\nAlthough OpenAI was reportedly [initially targeting](https://www.reuters.com/business/openai-lays-groundwork-juggernaut-ipo-up-1-trillion-valuation-2025-10-29/) a launch during 2026, following difficulties in reaching a \\$1T valuation, and the substantial decline of SpaceX's value following its IPO, [reporting now](https://www.forbes.com/sites/aliciapark/2026/06/25/openai-considers-delaying-ipo-to-2027-after-spacexs-rocky-debut-report-says/) indicates that the likely IPO has been delayed to 2027.",
